   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hypothesis\n",
    "\n",
    "We hypothesize that higher instructional funding per student will be positively associated with median graduate earnings approximately ten years after enrollment. Better-resourced institutions may be able to provide stronger instruction, student support, and career preparation, which could contribute to stronger long-term labor market outcomes. We expect this positive association to remain even after accounting for institutional size, region, and regional economic conditions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project uses publicly available administrative datasets from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), the U.S. Department of Education College Scorecard, and the U.S. Census Bureau American Community Survey (ACS).\n",
    "\n",
    "We combined three sources of data:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. IPEDS institutional finance and enrollment data for public colleges  \n",
    "2. College Scorecard earnings and geographic identifiers  \n",
    "3. American Community Survey (ACS) state-level median household income  \n",
    "\n",
    "Detailed cleaning, tidying, and merging steps were completed in the Data Checkpoint notebook (`01-DataCheckpoint.ipynb`), while exploratory analyses were completed in the EDA Checkpoint notebook (`02-EDACheckpoint.ipynb`). In this report we load the processed datasets from `data/02-processed/` and summarize only the variables and analyses used in the final model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Dataset 1 — Merged IPEDS Finance and College Scorecard Earnings (2012)\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset contains institution-level finance, enrollment, and earnings data created by merging IPEDS institutional finance data with College Scorecard earnings data using the `UNITID` identifier. Each row represents one public institution. This merged dataset corresponds to Dataset 1 from the Data Checkpoint and serves as the primary analytic dataset for the final project.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key variables:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `instruction_exp_2012` — instructional expenditures (USD)  \n",
    "- `enrollment_2012` — total enrollment  \n",
    "- `funding_per_student_2012` — instructional expenditures divided by enrollment  \n",
    "- `MD_EARN_WNE_P10` — median earnings approximately 10 years after enrollment  \n",
    "\n",
    "Funding per student is used instead of total expenditures to account for institutional size differences.\n",
    "\n",
    "This merged dataset was created during the Data Checkpoint, saved to  `data/02-processed/merged_ipeds2012_scorecard2012_13.csv`,  and loaded directly in the final analysis."
   ]
