    "### Dataset 3 — ACS State Median Household Income\n",
    "\n",
    "State-level income data from the American Community Survey (ACS) were used as a proxy for regional economic conditions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key variable:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `median_household_income` — median household income by state\n",
    "\n",
    "The ACS data were cleaned during the Data Checkpoint using helper functions defined in `modules/acs_processing.py`, converted to a long format with state abbreviations, and saved to `data/02-processed/acs_median_income_2012_long.csv` This dataset is merged with the institutional dataset using the `STABBR` state abbreviation variable in order to control for regional economic differences in the regression analysis."
   ]
